# Taksh E-Commerce — local environment (NOT committed; see .env.example)
# Only keys the app actually reads at runtime are listed here.

# Google Places API key — address search suggestions in the map picker.
# Enable "Places API" on this key in Google Cloud Console.
# Use a SEPARATE key from the Android Maps key: this one is sent from the app over plain HTTP, so it
# cannot use Android package/SHA-1 restrictions. Restrict it to "Places API" only, set quota limits and
# billing alerts in Google Cloud Console. CI uses the GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY secret.
# The Android Maps SDK key is NOT in this file: set MAPS_API_KEY as an environment variable, or in
# android/local.properties (git-ignored), or pass -PMAPS_API_KEY=... to Gradle.
# Client-side values ONLY: this file is bundled into the app. Never add server secrets here.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
